# A plain function from dynamics to an event: `fn !Changes $a, $b = !Updated ($a + $b)`
# (Type System ch. 4: `!Updated` takes its dynamic whole; Semantics ch. 7: a dynamic's
# update event fires in a tick in which the dynamic was recomputed, with the value after
# the tick). No firing reaches the body to lift it over, so the function takes its
# dynamics whole. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

!Changes: fn $Nat, $Nat -> !Nat
fn !Changes $a, $b = !Updated ($a + $b)

@page: @unit
@page:
    !bump <- Ui.Button($label=$"bump")                           # 0
    $count <- 0 then $count + 1 on !bump
    let !changed = !Changes $count, $count
    $seen <- 0 then !changed
    Ui.Label($text=$"{$seen}")                                   # 1
